# Copy to .env for local development. On Vercel, set the same keys under
# Settings → Environment Variables (they are read at BUILD time, so a change
# requires a redeploy to take effect).
#
# Everything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the client bundle and is therefore
# PUBLIC. Never put a secret, an API key or a signing key here.

# Base URL of the .NET API. LEAVE IT EMPTY — do not delete the key, an absent variable makes
# apiClient fall back to http://localhost:5043 and ships a production bundle calling localhost.
#
# Empty means "same origin": the frontend reaches the API through the /api, /hubs and /health
# rewrites declared in vercel.json, which proxy to the App Service. That is what makes the session
# cookie first-party, and it is the only arrangement mobile browsers accept — WebKit's ITP, Firefox's
# Total Cookie Protection and Chrome's third-party phase-out all block cross-site cookies by default,
# so an absolute URL here restores direct cross-site calls and breaks login on every phone.
VITE_API_URL=

# Where the Vite dev server proxies /api, /hubs and /health. Defaults to a locally running API;
# set it to the deployed App Service URL to develop against it. Development goes through the proxy
# for the same reason production does: the cookie must stay first-party on localhost:5173.
VITE_DEV_API_TARGET=http://localhost:5043

# Local AI engine (Ollama) used for offline clinical-report generation. It is the ONLY generation
# path: there is no server-side fallback. An earlier build had one and it was removed — sending
# clinical notes to a remote model is exactly what this feature exists to avoid. When the runtime is
# unreachable the feature reports itself unavailable (with the reason) and the clinician writes the
# report by hand; nothing is generated elsewhere.
#
# Consequence for deployment: the clinician's machine MUST run Ollama with the model below, or she
# loses the feature entirely. Light devices (phones, tablets) never have it.
#
# 127.0.0.1 rather than localhost: Ollama binds IPv4 by default, while localhost may resolve to ::1
# first, and the two spellings are not treated identically by every browser's local-network policy.
#
# The clinician's Ollama must allow this application's origin, otherwise the browser discards the
# response. On their machine:
#   OLLAMA_ORIGINS=https://app.juliette-marechal.be  (or http://localhost:5173 in development)
VITE_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
VITE_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# NOTE — handwriting recognition needs no variable here. MyScript is called by the API, not by the
# browser: its application key and HMAC key are secrets, and an HMAC key exists precisely to prove a
# request comes from the server, so publishing it in this bundle would defeat its purpose. They are
# configured on the API instead (Azure: Handwriting__ApplicationKey, Handwriting__HmacKey).
# If you still have VITE_MYSCRIPT_APP_KEY / VITE_MYSCRIPT_HMAC_KEY in a local .env, delete them.
